    <item>
      <title>hey look what&#39;s staring back at you</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/ostrava-solo/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Feb 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/ostrava-solo/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solo exhibition at Galerie Provoz, Ostrava&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img
    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;
    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
    decoding=&#34;async&#34;
    fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;
    alt=&#34;&#34;
    src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/ostrava-exhib2.png&#34;
    &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img
    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;
    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
    decoding=&#34;async&#34;
    fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;
    alt=&#34;&#34;
    src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/ostrava-exhib1.png&#34;
    &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Text by curator Dominika Goralska
    &lt;div id=&#34;text-by-curator-dominika-goralska&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#text-by-curator-dominika-goralska&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;
    
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you see that reflection? The one staring back at you. Something about it is suspiciously familiar. Maybe it moves like you, maybe it reminds you of something. Or you simply become part of its existence. It is not a hallucination, but an inevitable truth: the viewer is never just an observer.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Denle Chayote</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/video/denle-chayote/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 15 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/video/denle-chayote/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;vimeo-responsive &#34; style=&#34;margin: 2rem 0;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;iframe src=&#34;https://player.vimeo.com/video/910960727?responsive=1&#34;
          frameborder=&#34;0&#34;
          allow=&#34;autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture&#34;
          allowfullscreen&gt;
  &lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
.vimeo-responsive {
  position: relative;
  padding-bottom: 56.25%;
  height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  max-width: 1067px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

.vimeo-responsive iframe {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.vimeo-responsive.portrait {
  padding-bottom: 177.78%;
  max-width: 450px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

.vimeo-responsive.square {
  padding-bottom: 100%;
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .vimeo-responsive.portrait,
  .vimeo-responsive.square {
    max-width: 90%;
  }
}
&lt;/style&gt;

This work is an attempt to delve into the complexities of identity, culture, and human connection while drawing inspiration from the narrative styles of TV and YouTube shows. Through the humanised character of a chayote, I explore themes of post-colonialism and cultural exchange, primarily inspired by my experiences in Oaxaca, Mexico. With a blend of humour and introspection, the viewer is invited to join me on a personal journey of exchange, fostering a deeper understanding of the shared human experience.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Orientalism(not) feat. Edward Said</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/said/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 08 Jan 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/said/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;supporting text for the &lt;a
  href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/projects/video/orientalism-not/&#34;&gt;video essay&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;div id=&#34;supporting-text-for-the-video-essay&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#supporting-text-for-the-video-essay&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;
    
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I first came across the term &amp;lsquo;Orientalism&amp;rsquo; while reading about a controversial photograph that won an award by National Geographic in 2016. I learnt about rampant racism and stereotyping that has been taking place not just in photojournalism but in every quarter of media and culture. This led to me finding out about Edward Said and his work.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
